1. Control Plane components

These manage the Kubernetes cluster:

Control Plane
│
├── API Server
├── etcd
├── Scheduler
└── Controller Manager
API Server → receives kubectl commands and API requests.
etcd → stores Kubernetes cluster information/state.
Scheduler → decides which Worker Node should run a new Pod.
Controller Manager → continuously makes the actual state match the desired state.
2. Worker Node components

These run your application Pods:

Worker Node
│
├── kubelet
├── kube-proxy
├── Container Runtime
└── Pods
kubelet → manages Pods on that node.
kube-proxy → helps provide Kubernetes Service networking.
Container Runtime → actually runs containers, such as containerd or CRI-O.
Pods → run your application containers.
3. Common Kubernetes add-ons/components

You may see these in kube-system:

kube-system
│
├── CoreDNS
├── kube-proxy
├── Metrics Server
├── CNI networking components
└── Cloud/cluster-specific components
CoreDNS → provides DNS inside the cluster.
Metrics Server → provides CPU/memory metrics for kubectl top and HPA.
CNI plugin → provides Pod networking. Examples include Calico, Cilium, and others.
kube-proxy → Service networking.
