5. Why doesn't Kubernetes directly run the container?
Because Kubernetes uses the Pod as the unit of scheduling and management.
For example, Scheduler says:  Put nginx Pod on Worker Node 1
Not:  Put nginx container on Worker Node 1
Then kubelet on Node 1 makes sure that Pod exists, and the container runtime runs the container(s) inside it.




